.TH BUCKLE\-X11 "1" "October 2026" "Bucklespring keyboard sound" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
buckle\-x11 \- Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound, X11 flavour
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buckle-x11
[\fI\,options\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Buckle emulates the sound of an old IBM Model-M space saver
bucklespring keyboard while typing within an X session.
.PP
It runs as a background process and plays back the sound of each key
pressed and released on the keyboard, just as if using an IBM Model-M.
The sound of each key has carefully been sampled, and is played back
while simulating the proper distance and direction for a realistic 3D
sound palette of pure nostalgic bliss.
.PP
This flavour grabs key events through X11, and therefore only reports keys
typed within an X session.  For Wayland compositors and for the console, see
.BR buckle\-libinput (1).
.PP
The mouse clicks too: the buttons, and the scroll wheel, one click per detent.
Use
.B \-\-no\-click
to silence it, or to silence only some of it.
.PP
A key held down long enough to repeat clicks for every repeat.  The X server
does not repeat the modifier keys, so holding shift stays quiet by itself.

Where it was built with the system tray, and there is a tray to put it in, an
icon appears there with a menu for pausing, the volume, the output device and
quitting.  The volume is a submenu of levels with
.B +
and
.B \-
at the ends of it, and rolling the wheel over the icon changes it without
opening the menu at all.
.B \-\-no\-tray
leaves it out.  The icon is a StatusNotifierItem, which KDE Plasma shows as it
is and GNOME Shell shows through an extension; where nothing is listening
there is simply no icon and nothing else changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR=\fI\,DEVICE\/\fR
use OpenAL audio device DEVICE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fallback\-sound\fR
use a fallback sound for unknown keys
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-gain\fR=\fI\,GAIN\/\fR
set playback gain [0..100]
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mute\-keycode\fR=\fI\,CODE\/\fR
use CODE as mute key (default 0x46 for scroll lock)
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-mute\fR
start the program muted
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-no\-click\fR[=\fI\,LIST\/\fR]
don't play a sound on mouse click; LIST
narrows it to some of left, middle, right,
side, extra, wheel, hwheel, all, none
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show help
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\-devices\fR
list available OpenAL audio devices
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-audio\-path\fR=\fI\,PATH\/\fR
load .wav files from directory PATH
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-no\-repeat\fR
stay silent while a held key auto repeats
.TP
\fB\-\-repeat\-delay\fR=\fI\,MS\/\fR
wait MS before the first repeat, overriding
what the compositor or the kernel says
.TP
\fB\-\-repeat\-rate\fR=\fI\,HZ\/\fR
make HZ repeats per second, likewise
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-stereo\-width\fR=\fI\,WIDTH\/\fR
set stereo width [0..100]
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tray\fR
do not put an icon in the system tray
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
increase verbosity / debugging
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
show version and exit
